  <notes-header>

  <chapter*|What's new>

  <notes-abstract|New and updated content on these pages, most recent first: writings, lecture notes, talks and papers.>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|5 November 2026> \<cdot\> <with|font-shape|italic|paper><next-line><with|font-series|bold|Nonlinear PDEs with modulated dispersion II: Korteweg\Ude Vries equation>

    With K.<nbsp>Chouk, G.<nbsp>Li, J.<nbsp>Li and T.<nbsp>Oh, accepted for publication in the Memoirs of the European Mathematical Society (<hlink|arXiv:1406.7675|https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.7675>). See the <notes-link|publications|research/publications.tm> page.
  </notes-news-item>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|5 November 2026> \<cdot\> <with|font-shape|italic|lectures><next-line><with|font-series|bold|<notes-link|A constructive introduction to quantum field theory|teaching/lectures-constructive-qft-sissa-2026.tm>>

    Notes and slides (PDF, HTML and TeXmacs sources) of my course at SISSA, Trieste, 20 October\U9 November 2026. Lectures<nbsp>1\U5 have been delivered. The provisional materials for Lectures<nbsp>6\U7 give an FBSDE construction of <math|\<phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> on the torus, with new results from joint work with Sarah-Jean Meyer. <with|font-shape|italic|Course page added 21 October 2026; updated 5 November 2026.>
  </notes-news-item>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|30 October 2026> \<cdot\> <with|font-shape|italic|lectures><next-line><with|font-series|bold|<notes-link|A stochastic analysis perspective on Euclidean fields|teaching/lectures-euclidean-fields-st-flour-2025.tm>>

    Lecture notes and the eight recordings of my course at the 53rd Saint-Flour Probability Summer School (2025), with timestamps linking to each topic. The <notes-link|teaching|teaching/teaching.tm> page now also lists my lecture series.
  </notes-news-item>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|27 October 2026> \<cdot\> <with|font-shape|italic|talk><next-line><with|font-series|bold|Stochastic observables and the forward\Ubackward flow of a Euclidean field>

    Workshop <hlink|Deterministic and Stochastic Evolution Equations|https://indico.sns.it/event/149/>, Scuola Normale Superiore, Pisa (<notes-store|slides|talk-pisa-observables-fbsde-2026.pdf>). The <notes-link|presentations|research/presentations.tm#sec:slides> archive also has new slides from the SISSA workshop (September 28\UOctober 2, 2026) and from York (March 11, 2026).
  </notes-news-item>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|23 October 2026> \<cdot\> <with|font-shape|italic|writing><next-line><with|font-series|bold|<notes-link|What do we talk about when we talk about unbounded self-adjoint operators?|zettels/self-adjoint-operators.tm>>

    The first post of a series that uses the notion of an observable as an organising principle for the theory of unbounded self-adjoint operators: spectral measures, resolvents, unitary groups and strong resolvent convergence. A companion page gives the <notes-link|proofs and complements|zettels/self-adjoint-operators-proofs.tm>.
  </notes-news-item>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|12 October 2026> \<cdot\> <with|font-shape|italic|paper><next-line><with|font-series|bold|Parabolic stochastic quantisation of the fractional <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> model in the full subcritical regime>

    With P.<nbsp>Duch and P.<nbsp>Rinaldi, published online in the <hlink|Journal of the European Mathematical Society|https://doi.org/10.4171/JEMS/1816> (<hlink|arXiv:2303.18112|https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.18112>).
  </notes-news-item>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|September 2026> \<cdot\> <with|font-shape|italic|paper><next-line><with|font-series|bold|Constructive stochastic quantisation>

    My lecture notes from the CIME school \PStatistical Mechanics and Stochastic PDEs\Q (Cetraro, 2023), forthcoming in Springer's Lecture Notes in Mathematics, vol.<nbsp>2401.
  </notes-news-item>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|2 September 2026> \<cdot\> <with|font-shape|italic|talk><next-line><with|font-series|bold|Stochastic observables and constructive RG>

    Invited plenary talk at the <hlink|13th International Conference on the Exact Renormalization Group (ERG2026)|https://indico.global/event/16125/contributions/164437/>, University of Sussex, Brighton (<notes-store|slides|stochastic-observables-wilson-ito-sussex-beamer.pdf>).
  </notes-news-item>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|July 2026> \<cdot\> <with|font-shape|italic|papers><next-line><with|font-series|bold|Nonlinear PDEs with modulated dispersion>

    Part<nbsp>IV, <em|Normal form approach and unconditional uniqueness> (with G.<nbsp>Li, J.<nbsp>Li and T.<nbsp>Oh), published in the <hlink|Peking Mathematical Journal|https://doi.org/10.1007/s42543-026-00123-8>. Two new preprints: Part<nbsp>III, <em|Multiplicative noises> (with A.<nbsp>Chapouto, G.<nbsp>Li, J.<nbsp>Li and T.<nbsp>Oh, <hlink|arXiv:2607.08385|https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.08385>), and <em|Refined global well-posedness for the periodic modulated Korteweg\Ude Vries equation> (with D.<nbsp>Greco, S.<nbsp>Liu and T.<nbsp>Oh, <hlink|arXiv:2607.09023|https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.09023>).
  </notes-news-item>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|January 2026> \<cdot\> <with|font-shape|italic|preprint><next-line><with|font-series|bold|On the weak coupling limit of the periodic quantum Lorentz gas>

    With V.<nbsp>Sanjay (<hlink|arXiv:2601.07453|https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.07453>).
  </notes-news-item>

  For everything else, see the <notes-link|writings|zettels/writings.tm>, <notes-link|teaching|teaching/teaching.tm>, <notes-link|presentations|research/presentations.tm> and <notes-link|publications|research/publications.tm> pages, the <notes-link|list|list-articles.tm> of all the articles and the <notes-link|Atom|notes.atom> feed.
